.el .ds Aq '
.TH ferry-config 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-config \- Show or change settings (`ferry config list`, `get`, `set`, `unset`, `path`), or check and repair the configuration file (`check`, `repair`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry config\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or change settings (`ferry config list`, `get`, `set`, `unset`, `path`), or check and repair the configuration file (`check`, `repair`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ferry\-config\-list(1)
Show every setting
.TP
ferry\-config\-get(1)
Show one setting
.TP
ferry\-config\-set(1)
Change one setting
.TP
ferry\-config\-unset(1)
Reset one setting to its default
.TP
ferry\-config\-path(1)
Print the path of the configuration file
.TP
ferry\-config\-check(1)
Check the configuration file for damage and for settings someone else may have changed; exits with an error when it is damaged
.TP
ferry\-config\-repair(1)
Repair a damaged configuration file: what can be read is kept, a copy of the old file is saved next to it
